# Kill list — plain terms. Edit like a shopping list: one banned word or phrase per line.
# No regex. The scanner supplies the matching:
#   [words]   -> whole word, any case, with universal inflections (s/es/ed/ing/ly, e-drop)
#   [phrases] -> matched literally anywhere, any case, apostrophes/quotes normalised
# Lines starting with # are comments. A [section] in brackets sets the match mode.
# Exceptions (e.g. "move" for literal motion, "name" in a heading) are judgement —
# the scanner flags them NEEDS-JUDGEMENT and a person decides. See kill-list.md for the why.

[words]
structural
substrate
move
fill
load-bearing
name

[phrases]
it's important to note
it's worth mentioning
that's a great question
for one reason or another
it turns out that
i keep coming back to
the question that won't let me go
the thing i want to sit with
i want to be careful here
i'll flag honestly
let me be precise
to be exact
the same
this is fundamental
this is systemic
this is essential
as we'll see
in what follows
this section
